---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Figure from "../components/Figure.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
---

<Layout title={`Research guide — ${site.wordmark}`}>
  <div class="reading-container">
    <header class="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">{site.venue}</p><h1>Research guide</h1><p class="lead">
        {site.title}
      </p><p>{site.guideIntro}</p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button dark" href={site.paperUrl}>Published paper ↗</a>{
          site.htmlPaper && (
            <a class="button" href={site.htmlPaper}>
              Full preprint in HTML ↗
            </a>
          )
        }{
          site.pdfUrl && (
            <a class="button" href={site.pdfUrl}>
              {site.pdfLabel} ↗
            </a>
          )
        }
      </div>
    </header>
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="Research guide contents">
      <h2>In this guide</h2><ol>
        <li><a href="#guide-flying-dna">Flying DNA and the published study</a></li>
        {
          site.guideSections.map((section, i) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#guide-${i + 1}`}>{section.title}</a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <section id="guide-flying-dna">
        <h2>Flying DNA and the published study</h2>
        <p>
          The six-slide Flying DNA project presentation places advanced air
          mobility within a broader research vision: digital twins represent
          environments and systems, networked systems connect physical agents
          and infrastructure, and artificial intelligence supports understanding,
          design, and control. Slides 5–6 illustrate directions in urban wind
          sensing, prediction, and aerial navigation.
        </p>
        <p>
          The published 2025 study below evaluates a specific part of that
          vision: modified PPO learns multi-objective eVTOL motion in a simulated
          city with computed CFD wind fields. The broader presentation does not
          add a quantitative benchmark or establish an operational sensing
          network, online wind prediction, or real-flight validation for this
          planner. All reported numbers and technical details continue to follow
          the published article.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a separately attributed reference, see
          <a href={asset("#related-work")}
            >GeoWind2Plan in the homepage’s independent related work</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="fine-print">
          Presentation source: Flying DNA, slides 2–3 (program framework) and
          5–6 (wind and navigation illustrations). The original presentation and
          published paper remain unchanged.
        </p>
      </section>
      <Fragment>
        {
          site.guideSections.map((section, i) => (
            <section id={`guide-${i + 1}`}>
              <h2>{section.title}</h2>
              {section.paragraphs.map((p) => (
                <p>{p}</p>
              ))}
            </section>
          ))
        }
      </Fragment>
      <section>
        <h2>Boundaries of the evidence</h2><ul>
          {site.limitations.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
    <Figure id={site.id === "mixed_traffic" ? "network" : "wind"} />
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Continue with the evidence</h2><p>
        <a href={asset("results/")}
          >Read the original figure descriptions and numeric results</a
        >, including downloadable CSV tables.
      </p><p><a href={site.repo}>{site.repoLabel}</a>. {site.repoNote}</p><p
        class="fine-print"
      >
        The uploaded publisher PDF was used to verify this guide and extract the
        original figures. It remains unchanged. External publisher PDFs and the
        arXiv preprint have not been certified for accessibility; <a
          href={asset("accessibility/#attachments")}
          >read the attachment notes</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
